# 108 · Gated models on cloud rigs

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.1.4](../roadmap.md#v014)

## What

A plan only; nothing of it is built.

A rig launched on a GPU cloud can import a gated model, one whose source needs the owner's token (a gated model on Hugging Face, for example), as a rig on a machine or a cluster can with `THERMITE_HF_TOKEN_FILE`. Control gives the pod the token at launch as a launch value it keeps no copy of, as it does the snapshot key, held only by the part of the rig that fetches models and never reachable by agents; the isolation self-test checks that no other role can read it. The launch page says which models it allows, and a launch without it says why a gated import fails.

## Why

A RunPod launch gives the pod no token for a gated model source, so a campaign that needs a gated model can't run on a RunPod rig. Found on 2026-10-23 while the docs were checked against the goals: the RunPod page's note on gated models pointed to a goal already verified, with no plan left for the gap.

## Done when

- [ ] Written when the goal is accepted into a version.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-24, owner: v0.1.1 becomes the code clean-up; this goal moves to v0.1.3.

## Open questions

- Whether control keeps the token for later launches (a secret in Settings, per cloud account) or the owner gives it at each launch.

## Progress

- 2026-10-23: Goal written as a plan, from the docs check.

